          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In elementary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bayes%27+formula"} Bayes' formula
            refers to a version of the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P(A)\,P(B|A) \,=\, P(B)\,P(A|B)
                  \\,,
          %p
            and relates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+probability"} conditional probability
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the one of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            given
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            From the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category-theoretic+probability"} category-theoretic point of view
            = succeed "," do
              %strong Bayesian inversion
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger structure
          %h2#intuition Intuition
          %p
            In logical reasoning, implications in general cannot be reversed:
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
            which is absent in pure logical reasoning.
          %p
            Consider for example a city in which
            = succeed "." do
              %em all taxis are yellow
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi taxi
                    %mo →
                    %mi yellow
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} taxi\to yellow
            %em more likely
            that it’s a taxi compared to a randomly colored car. This increase in likelihood is larger if the fraction of yellow cars is small. Indeed,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bayes%27+rule"} Bayes' rule
            says that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi taxi
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi yellow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi taxi
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi taxi
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P(taxi|yellow) = \frac{P(yellow\,taxi)}{P(yellow)} = \frac{P(taxi)}{P(yellow)} .
          %p
            More generally, in a city where
            %em most
            taxis are yellow, there is a high conditional probability that a given taxi is yellow,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi yellow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi taxi
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P(yellow|taxi) .
          %p
            The higher this probability is, the higher is the probability that a given yellow car is a taxi, again according to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bayes%27+rule"} Bayes' rule
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi taxi
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi yellow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi taxi
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi taxi
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi taxi
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi yellow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P(taxi|yellow) = \frac{P(yellow\,taxi)}{P(yellow)} = \frac{P(taxi)\,P(yellow|taxi)}{P(yellow)}
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+probability"} categorical probability
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi taxi
                  %mo ,
                  %mi not
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi taxi
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi colors
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi of
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi cars
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{taxi, not\,taxi\}\to\{colors\,of\,cars\}
            there corresponds a canonical morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi colors
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi of
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi cars
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi taxi
                    %mo ,
                    %mi not
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi taxi
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{colors\,of\,cars\}\to\{taxi, not\,taxi\}
            = succeed "." do
              %em Bayesian inverse
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+morphism"} inverse morphism
            in the sense of category theory, but simply a reversal of the arrow.
          %p
            In some cases, this symmetry gives rise to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger category
          %h2#in_traditional_probability_theory In traditional probability theory
          %p
            In traditional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+probability"} conditional probability
          %h3#discrete_case Discrete case
          %p
            In the discrete case, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+distribution"} probability distribution
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is simply a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:X\to[0,1]
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{x\in X} p(x) = 1 .
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+map"} stochastic map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k:X\to Y
