          %p
            This recovers the classical probability definitions when instantiated in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
            and its subcategories.
          %p
            Just as in traditional probability, Bayesian inverses are unique only up to
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                almost sure equality
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/almost+sure+equality"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category#conditionals"} conditionals
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BorelStoch"} BorelStoch
          %p
            (See also
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category#conditionals"} Markov category - conditionals
          %h3#in_dagger_categories In dagger categories
          %p
            In the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+couplings"} category of couplings
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+spaces"} probability spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{A},p)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\mathcal{B},q)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+%28probability+theory%29"} coupling
            between them can be seen equivalently as going from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            or from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernels"} Markov kernels
          %p
            Categorical abstractions of the category of coupling via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+categories"} dagger categories
            have therefore the concept of Bayesian inversion already built in.
          %h2#quantum_versions Quantum versions
          %p (For now, see the references.)
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+probability"}> categorical probability
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category"} Markov category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport+plan"}> transport plan
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+couplings"} category of couplings
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel"}> Markov kernel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+map"} stochastic map
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+probability"}> conditional probability
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+expectation"} conditional expectation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"}> probability theory
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistics"} statistics
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bayesian+statistics"} Bayesian statistics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger category
          %h2#references References
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+probability"} categorical probability
          %ul
            %li#fritzmarkov
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Fritz"}> Tobias Fritz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A synthetic approach to Markov kernels, conditional independence and theorems on sufficient statistics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07021"} arXiv:1908.07021
            %li#cd_categories
              %p
                Kenta Cho and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"} Bart Jacobs
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Disintegration and Bayesian Inversion via String Diagrams
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.00322"} arXiv:1709.00322
            %li
              %p
                Dario Stein and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sam+Staton"} Sam Staton
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Probabilistic Programming with Exact Conditions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.17141"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                Noé Ensarguet and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"} Paolo Perrone
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical probability spaces, ergodic decompositions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.04267"} arXiv:2310.04267
          %p For the quantum case:
          %ul
            %li#coecke_spekkens12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Coecke"}> Bob Coecke
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+W.+Spekkens"} Robert W. Spekkens
              = succeed "," do
                %em Picturing classical and quantum Bayesian inference
              %strong 186
              3 (2012) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.2368"}> arXiv:1102.2368
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11229-011-9917-5"} doi:10.1007/s11229-011-9917-5
          %p
            and using
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+categories"} Markov categories
          %ul
            %li#quantum_markov
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"}> Arthur J. Parzygnat
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inverses, disintegrations, and Bayesian inversion in quantum Markov categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.08375"} arXiv
            %li#noncommutative_bayes
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"}> Arthur J. Parzygnat
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+P.+Russo"} Benjamin P. Russo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A noncommutative Bayes theorem
                %strong 644
                (2022) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.laa.2022.02.030"}> doi:10.1016/j.laa.2022.02.030
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.03886"} arXiv:2005.03886
            %li#conditional_quantum
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"}> Arthur J. Parzygnat
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conditional distributions for quantum systems
                %strong 343
                (2021) 1-13 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.01529"}> arXiv:2102.01529
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.343.1"} doi:10.4204/EPTCS.343.1
            %li#retrodiction
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"}> Arthur J. Parzygnat
                , Francesco Buscemi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Axioms for retrodiction: achieving time-reversal symmetry with a prior
                %strong 7
                (2023) 1013 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.13531"}> arXiv:2210.13531
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.22331/q-2023-05-23-1013"} doi:10.22331/q-2023-05-23-1013
            %li#quantum_states_time
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Fullwood"}> James Fullwood
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"} Arthur J. Parzygnat
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On quantum states over time
                %strong 478
                (2022) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03607"}> arXiv:2202.03607
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.2022.0104"} doi:10.1098/rspa.2022.0104
            %li#quantum_bayes
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Fullwood"}> James Fullwood
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"} Arthur J. Parzygnat
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From time-reversal symmetry to quantum Bayes rules
                %strong 4
                020334 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.08088"}> arXiv:2212.08088
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PRXQuantum.4.020334"} doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.4.020334
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Fullwood"}> James Fullwood
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"} Arthur J. Parzygnat
                %em Operator representation of spatiotemporal quantum correlations
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.17555"}> arXiv:2405.17555
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"}> Arthur J. Parzygnat
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Fullwood"} James Fullwood
                %em Time-symmetric correlations for open quantum systems
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.11123"}> arXiv:2407.11123
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#noncomm_disintegrations
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+J.+Parzygnat"}> Arthur J. Parzygnat
                , Benjamin P. Russo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-commutative disintegrations: existence and uniqueness in finite dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.09689"} arXiv
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+Parzygnat"}> Arthur Parzygnat
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Spatiotemporal Extension of Density Matrices and Time-Reversal Symmetry for Measurements
              %a{:href => "Center+for+Quantum+and+Topological+Systems#ParzygnatNov2024"} talk at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
              (Nov 2024) &amp;lbrack;slides:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Parzygnat-CQTS-Nov2024.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/probability"} probability
